# Root .dockerignore — applies to every build whose context is "." (currently just
# apps/backend's Dockerfile, see docker-compose.yml). Keeps the build context small and, more
# importantly, keeps apps/mobile (a completely separate app, never built into this image) and
# every workspace's own node_modules out of it — apps/backend/Dockerfile explicitly COPYs only
# the package.json files + source it actually needs (apps/backend, packages/shared-types).
node_modules
**/node_modules
apps/mobile
apps/web
apps/backend/dist
apps/backend/.env
apps/backend/.env.*
packages/shared-types/dist
# Stale local incremental-build caches — if copied in without their matching dist/ output
# (which is excluded above), tsc/nest build reads them, believes it's already up to date, and
# silently skips emitting anything. Bit us once already getting this Dockerfile working.
**/*.tsbuildinfo
.git
.next
docs
infra
*.md
